<title>UK: CE confirms offer for Northern unconditional.</title>
<headline>CE confirms offer for Northern unconditional.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S.-owned CE Electric on Friday confirmed its offer for British utility Northern Electric Plc was unconditional, adding that it now owned 50.30 percent of Northern.  </p>
<p>CE said it owned or had acceptances for 51.08 million ordinary shares of Northern at 1300 GMT on Tuesday, the final deadline for its offer.</p>
<p>CE declared victory after a knife-edge fight for Northern, which became the tenth of 12 privatised Regional Electricity Companies (RECs) to succumb to a takeover.</p>
<p>Only Yorkshire Electricity Plc and Southern Electric Plc now remain independent.</p>
